---
title: "Free Tool to Remove API Keys From Logs and Code"
description: "Remove API keys, tokens, passwords, private keys and internal hostnames from logs, config files and code before you share them. Runs in your browser."
faq:
  - q: "Is the Secrets Scrubber free?"
    a: "Yes. The tool is free, with no account, no sign-up and no limit on how often you use it."
  - q: "Is my text uploaded to a server?"
    a: "No. The page has no server code and uses no AI model. The pattern rules run in your browser, and your logs, config files and code never leave your device."
  - q: "Which secret formats does it find?"
    a: "More than 25 key and token formats, such as AWS, Stripe, GitHub, GitLab, Slack, Google, OpenAI, Anthropic, SendGrid, Twilio, npm, PyPI, Shopify, DigitalOcean and Hugging Face keys. It also finds JWTs, Bearer tokens, private key blocks, passwords, database connection strings, internal hostnames, IP and MAC addresses and emails."
  - q: "Will it find every secret?"
    a: "No. Pattern rules find keys with a known format and values next to names such as password, token or api_key. A random string with no known prefix and no name next to it can look like any other text. Always read the result before you share it, and add your own project names or hosts to the always-hide list."
  - q: "Should I rotate a leaked key?"
    a: "Yes. If a key was already shared, for example in a ticket, a chat or a public repository, removing it from the text does not make it safe again. Revoke the key with its provider and make a new one. Use the scrubber before you share, not after."
  - q: "Does it work offline?"
    a: "Yes. The tool uses no AI model and sends no requests while it works. Once the page has loaded, it can scrub text without a network connection."
  - q: "Can I use it before I paste logs into ChatGPT or an AI coding assistant?"
    a: "Yes. Choose numbered labels such as [API_KEY_1] and [API_KEY_2]. The same value gets the same label all through the text, so the assistant can still follow the logs without seeing your real keys."
  - q: "Can it remove keys from a screenshot or a screen recording?"
    a: "This tool is for plain text. For images, use the Screenshot Redactor, and for videos, use the Screencast Redactor. Both read the text on the screen and use the same key and password rules."
---

